id: DRAFT-tlfloat-1.15.0-ohos-cmake-probe-and-runtime-golden
title: HarmonyOS CMake feature probes and upstream runtime golden values need separate gates
path: B
category: cmake, toolchain, ohos, testing, conan
trigger_tool: cmake|clang|conan|ctest
error_signature: isnanl|isinfl|finitel|exp10|golden value|hash mismatch
root_cause: OHOS libc++ and runtime ABI do not provide all glibc long-double symbols or host-generated numeric golden values.
rec_approach: cache_variables plus static-library try_compile and an installed-package consumer gate
verification_cmd: conan create clean -pr:h=ohos-aarch64 -pr:b=ohos-aarch64 --build=missing -tf=test_package
evidence: HarmonyOS HongMeng Kernel 1.12.0 aarch64; upstream inventory 22 (12 selected and compiled, 7 passed/5 runtime-golden failed/10 optional disabled); consumer 8/8 assertions plus workflow 1/1 passed; CTest 2/2
forbid_1: silently report host-runtime golden failures as package failures without identifying the platform baseline
forbid_2: claim all upstream runtime tests passed when the device result is 7/12
similar_to: []
draft: true
